WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.533
The US Air

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.501
Force just released

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.002
new video

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.635
showing what

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.503
the Air Force calls

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.472
an unnecessarily aggressive maneuver

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.007
by a Chinese military pilot

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.109
right in front of a U.S. aircraft.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:09.676
CNN's Oren

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.177
Lieberman is live for us at the Pentagon.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.545
And tell us what happened.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.813
Jake, we're just getting this information

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.382
from U.S. Indo-Pacific command.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.850
They say a Chinese fighter

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.520
jet at J-16 on Friday intercepted a U.S.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.289
spy spy plane in international airspace

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.324
over the South China Sea.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:24.858
They're calling it

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.559
an unnecessarily aggressive maneuver

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.494
as part of the intercept.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.428
Take a look here.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.330
This is from the cockpit of the U.S.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.364
aircraft and RC one.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.266
35, that Chinese fighter

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.167
jet off to the right

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.269
there as it cuts in front,

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.303
essentially slices

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.138
right in front of the U.S.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.306
aircraft at fairly close range.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.141
And that turbulence

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.842
there, that is from wake turbulence

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.478
off the back of that Chinese fighter jet.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.446
Again, the U.S.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.347
is calling this

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.149
an aggressive maneuver

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.917
saying that it was essentially unsafe

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.918
and unprofessional.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.253
We have seen intercepts

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.220
like this,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.188
this sort of tension

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.157
between Chinese fighter jets and U.S.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.725
aircraft before, in fact,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.592
there was one in December,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.361
a different type of Chinese fighter jet,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.196
but essentially the same situation.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:03.696
The U.S.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.098
said that their fighter jet

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.133
came within 20 feet in that instance

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.268
of the same U.S.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.904
aircraft that RC one 35 river joint.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.672
The US position is clear here.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.206
They insist

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.607
they will continue to operate

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.776
in a safe and professional maneuver

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.710
anywhere, essentially

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.312
that international law allows.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.915
And therein lies the dispute for the U.S.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.616
airspace over much of the South China

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.418
Sea is international airspace

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.020
over international waters.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.088
China, however, claims

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.389
much of the South China Sea

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.357
as its own territorial waters

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.192
and therefore believes

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:32.992
that it is the U.S.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.894
invading on their territorial position.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:35.395
The U.S.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.796
does not recognize

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:37.864
it is at this point

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.799
one in a number of elements

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.501
or aspects, adding tension

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.469
to the relationship

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.737
between Beijing and Washington

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.238
at this point.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.106
And we're seeing that play out

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.807
in a different environment as well, Jake.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.175
Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.977
in the Indo-Pacific

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.112
for the Shangri-La Dialog.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.246
He was trying to set up a meeting

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.514
with his Chinese counterpart.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.683
China rejecting that dialog, Jake.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:57.517
So you see that

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.952
tension playing out across

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.553
different aspects of the relationship.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.455
What do you see when you look at this?

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.256
How dangerous is it?

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.392
Obviously, a very unprofessional

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.560
and dangerous act

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.828
by what appears to be

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.763
the j-16 fighter pilot.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.232
As soon as I saw this tape,

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:15.001
I was reminded the event back in 2001.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.371
We saw a Chinese J eight fighter aircraft

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.673
collide with the Navy P-3 aircraft

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.741
over the South China Sea.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.343
So in the same area,

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.210
the result was

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.712
the Chinese aircraft was destroyed,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.046
the pilot was killed.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.415
And we almost lost an entire aircraft

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.051
full of of American servicemen and women.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.954
Fortunately, they landed on Hainan Island

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.656
in Chinese territory.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.391
Now, imagine that was 20 years ago.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.693
Imagine that same event happening today

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.794
with the tensions

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.897
that we have between our two nations.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.031
Very dangerous.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.399
And the Chinese need to condemn it.

